Source: https://github.com/estkme-group/lpac, release v2.3.0
(commit c2fcf5e4b21c712d54e35a11da2ad9ad134fb821, archive SHA-256
f3e92f08d10121cf3633cce66853ba1260eb5daa35c594f903cc2720fc11f9ee).

The binary deployed as /data/u60-panel/lpac is built from that source with the patches
in scripts/lpac-patches/ (backports of upstream fixes and OpenUI's own changes,
each described in its header) by scripts/prepare-lpac.py, which pins the archive,
the patches and the Zig toolchain. Together these files are the binary's
corresponding build inputs. The local package also includes the exact source
archive in source/lpac-source.tar.gz; unpack it and apply the shipped patches
or use the SHA-256-pinned scripts/prepare-lpac.py.

Licenses, per lpac's REUSE.toml:
- src/, driver/, utils/: AGPL-3.0-only (AGPL-3.0-only.txt)
- euicc/ (libeuicc): LGPL-2.1-only (LGPL-2.1-only.txt), or ESTKME's commercial licence
- cjson/: MIT (cJSON-MIT.txt)

lpac is a separate program. The MIT-licensed eSIM worker starts it and talks to it
over its standard input and output; the agent's licence does not change lpac's.
